# Build context hygiene. Everything here is either irrelevant to the image or
# student output that would make builds non-reproducible.

# macOS / editor noise
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Instructor-only - not shipped inside the student image
instructor/
INSTRUCTOR-TEST.md
RISK-GUIDE.md
publish.sh

# Host-side launcher scripts - students run these OUTSIDE the container
setup/

# Written at RUN time by the lab and never carried in from the context:
#   estate.json        the generated telemetry, ~1.5 MB, rebuilt every run
#   collector.log      what arrived at the mock collector
#   detect-log.jsonl   the detect beat's log
#   limit-result.json  the prevent stub's measurements
#   evade-result.json  the evasive channel's verdict
#   *-results.txt      the runner's saved transcript
#
# detector.json is NOT here. It is the shipped detector configuration the
# student tunes - the threshold and the matching window - so it must be in the
# image. The Dockerfile COPYs it twice, once as itself and once as
# detector.default.json, so every run starts from the shipped (deliberately
# wrong) state. Lab 12 hit exactly this with its rule file, lab 13 with its
# policy file and lab 14 with its trust list.
#
# variants.json and record.txt are NOT here either. They are lab 7's measured
# artefacts, shipped as the evidence the detector reads.
estate.json
collector.log
detect-log.jsonl
limit-result.json
evade-result.json
*-results.txt

# Credentials
.env
*.pem
*.key
